                <pb facs="0922" n="834" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg834"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic">December 16,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay informs Mr. Leishman that Admiral Cotton has been instructed to convey
                    Consul Davis to Alexandretta when he desires to go. Regrets demanded should be
                    explicit, but not humiliating, and apology by the governor and the punishment of
                    the offending police may be accepted as sufficient.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
